From 1918b10b6c4e22da3f9f1ab307a84d6ec905b391 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 01:05:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(fog): transport resolved native command stacks

Retain complete PLAYER_FOG snapshots and resolve every layer against the connection-selected resource packs. Publish an immutable versioned snapshot only after join and channel negotiation, including empty resets and late registrations. Preserve distance units and colors without inferring field-level inheritance.

Native Bedrock 1.26.60.5 with BDS 1.26.60.6 (protocol 2225) confirms unsigned-count string-array snapshots, topmost matching-medium precedence, and water-only fallback to lower air settings. Keep the independent command feature separate from registry-only air color defaults. Focused tests cover ownership replacement, precedence, payload validation, registration, and empty resets.

BREAKING CHANGE: FogDefinition now includes an immutable distance map alongside its color map.
